\newlabel{fig:forward_bias}{{3}{14}{Pre-merge Forward Bias across interface variants. Each point shows the mean over the 10 pilot episodes for one interface variant. Broad global scaling drives all cells toward strongly positive forward placement, whereas the narrow and mixed variants reveal task-conditioned trade-offs. Positive values indicate forward placement of the virtual point in the counterpart-velocity frame, and negative values indicate lagging placement}{figure.caption.4}{}}
